AUDIO: 'Hey, what\'s up guys and welcome back to Ask NK. Today we\'re going to look at Auto Remesher and [clears throat] Auto Remesher is made available by Hugs In Ge. Hugs In Ge is a recent creator of Dust 3D which is something that we\'ve covered on the channel some time ago. Dust 3D is this beautiful yet simple tool that you can use to create 3D models by using nodes and this works'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'more like what you\'ve got with meatballs. And he has just put together Auto Remesher and Auto Remesher is a cross-platform automatic rectangular remeshing tool that simply converts high poly meshes into clean rectangular based topologies. And today we\'re simply going'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to take a look at this and also compare it with Blender. And something that just happened before we wrapped up the video is we did see a nice cool nugget that I think Blender artists would love which isn\'t from a phone add-on that communicates with Auto Remesher. And for'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'those who like to get this, all you need to do is go over to the link in the description. That\'ll bring you right here where you can read up on this. Now for those who like to compile this by themselves, of course, there are ways for you to simply clone the repository, build the C make and compile this for'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'both Windows, Mac and also Linux. But for those who like to just download these and get started with it, if you click on the releases, this is where things get interesting. Just in case it sounds familiar, it\'s possible that you\'ve heard about this tool before'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'because this tool has gone through years of iteration. Initially, this tool actually started out with a very unstable version, then we got the alpha 3 and then progressed to alpha 4, then they got to beta 1, then we\'ve got beta 2 and also beta 3 before this current'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'final release that we have here. And with this release, they re-licensed from the GPL version 3 to MIT. They\'ve also made some improvements, added adaptivity parameters, the sharp edge parameter, the smooth normal parameter, replaced'

[01:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'density with target quads parameter, added a command line interface, refined the main window theme and graphic widgets and also replaced the app icon. And with that said, we\'re simply going to go ahead and pop this open and take a'

